From: Zomdroid
Subject: [PATCH] zfa: answer LWJGL's GetProcAddress lookup

libzfa.so had no lookup function, so LWJGL resolved every GL function by name with dlsym and saw
only the static exports. Mesa implements and dispatches many more: 181 functions of OpenGL 4.0 and
later were NULL on a context that reports 4.6, and a mod calling glCreateTextures (Project
Viewpoint) aborted the JVM. libOSMesa.so never had the problem because it exports
OSMesaGetProcAddress, which is a call to _mesa_glapi_get_proc_address.

Export the same function from libzfa.so under the same name, one of the four LWJGL probes. No
launcher change is needed. 0004-timer-query-exports.patch becomes redundant but stays harmless.

---
diff --git a/src/gallium/frontends/zfa/zfa.c b/src/gallium/frontends/zfa/zfa.c
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/zfa/zfa.c
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/zfa/zfa.c
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 #include <kopper_interface.h>
 #include <vulkan/vulkan_android.h>
 #include "GL/zfa.h"
+#include "glapi/glapi.h"
 
 #include <threads.h>
 #include <frontend/api.h>
@@ -317,6 +318,23 @@
    return st_api_make_current(zfa->st, &zfa->current_surface->base, &zfa->current_surface->base);
 }
 
+typedef void (*ZFAproc)(void);
+
+/*
+ * LWJGL asks a GL library for a lookup function under four names: glXGetProcAddress,
+ * glXGetProcAddressARB, eglGetProcAddress and OSMesaGetProcAddress. Without one it resolves
+ * every GL function with dlsym, and only the functions in static_data.functions are exported,
+ * so the rest were NULL although the context implements them (181 functions of OpenGL 4.0+,
+ * glCreateTextures among them). Answer under the OSMesa name, the way libOSMesa does.
+ */
+GLAPI ZFAproc GLAPIENTRY OSMesaGetProcAddress(const char *funcName);
+
+GLAPI ZFAproc GLAPIENTRY
+OSMesaGetProcAddress(const char *funcName)
+{
+   return (ZFAproc) _mesa_glapi_get_proc_address(funcName);
+}
+
 GLAPI void GLAPIENTRY
 zfaFlushFront(void)
 {
